  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On the road toward Bai Gu mountain, Fang Yuan uses Earth Communication Ear Grass and finds burnt wood under a tree, then a stream battlefield of chopped trees, a shifted watercourse, and a hundred beast king skeleton. Later ground marks show cut-away flesh and an injury that worsens as he and Bai Ning Bing close the distance.",
      "chapters": [
        209
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_bai_gu_mountain",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "gu_earth_communication_ear_grass",
        "char_bai_ning_bing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She was a farmer who fell while plowing, found a corpse with an inheritance, and became a Gu Master out of the blue. A mountain leopard then wiped out her village and drove her into the wild. After half a year roaming, most of her Gu had already died. In her own view she remains a half-baked Gu Master, severely lacking foundations. Fang Yuan reads her rough accent, poor fighting tactics, and unconcealed blood trail as the mark of a farmer lucky enough to gain an inheritance, and names the buried explosion traps ahead of her shelter as rank two Charred Thunder Potato.",
      "chapters": [
        210
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master",
        "gu_charred_thunder_potato_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She is a middle-aged woman without shoes, with large feet and thick black fur growing on her soles. Her face and limbs have a peculiar green color from green python poison.",
      "chapters": [
        209
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Her body is tough and healthy, with large hands and feet.",
      "chapters": [
        210
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "While she fights a twin-headed boar, Bai Ning Bing closes in under stealth and kills her with the Chainsaw Golden Centipede. Fang Yuan then takes three Gu from the aperture (rice bag grass Gu, iron thorn thistle Gu, and a charred thunder bean mother Gu), plus hairy leg Gu and jumping grass Gu from the body. A bookworm in the smashed head is already dead. A silver triangle tattoo marks Third Watch Gu on her chest. That expendable rank five Gu made her time run three times as fast, so her aperture nurture and primeval essence recovery ran three times as fast, and so did the poison’s worsening. Fang Yuan reads her as A grade talent, not a ten extreme physique.",
      "chapters": [
        211
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
